  "findings": "The adopted 2026–2027 regulations and exact Dutch prospectus establish 180 EC. The first year contains twelve required 5 EC courses. The later years contain nine required 5 EC courses and the 15 EC Bachelor Project. At least 20 EC of specialisation and enough Psychology electives to reach 30 EC are required, alongside 30 EC of open study in this illustration. Both selected specialisation courses require passing all first-year courses. The standard Bachelor Project requires passing year one and Multivariate Data Analysis. Students work in a research team and are assessed on a research article, presentation and the research and collaboration process.",
  "authority": "Adopted 11 May 2026, effective September 2026; OER arts. 3.1 and 3.2 and Appendix 1. The browser-indexed official English PDF is readable even though the raw download returned an access block. Exact current Dutch course records confirm all individual credits and the capstone. The annual catalogue allocates 15 plus 25 EC across later-year elective groups; the formal OER controls the programme-wide split of specialisation, Psychology electives and open study. The current career course is 6462PS6PCY, counted once. The second career code and extra programme listing do not have annual credit-bearing module records."
}
